;; FH-ROUTELINK-005 — no routing artefact, no silent dead link.
;;
;; Routing is optional. The tempting failure is to render the anchor
;; anyway with an empty or missing href: the page looks finished, the
;; link does nothing, and the programmer learns about it from a user. So
;; the missing-hook check happens AT RENDER, before any anchor exists,
;; and it fails loud with a named id that says which artefact is missing,
;; where to get it, and which link asked.
;;
;; The id is pinned, not the message: a message is stable in meaning,
;; never in bytes.
{:fh/id "FH-ROUTELINK-005"
 :fh/law
 "Rendering a v/route-link without the routing artefact raises the named :rf.error/routing-artefact-missing at render — naming the view and the link's :to — rather than emitting a dead anchor."

 ;; The unpublished hook that makes the artefact absent.
 :hook :routing/link-model

 :error
 {:id       :rf.error/routing-artefact-missing
  ;; ex-data slots a tool and a reader both need.
  :where    v/route-link
  :recovery :no-recovery
  ;; The link that asked, so the diagnostic points at a site and not just
  ;; at the framework.
  :to       :fh.route/cart}

 ;; Substrings the human sentence must carry: the artefact to add and the
 ;; namespace to require. Substring, not equality — the sentence is prose.
 :message-mentions ["day8/re-frame2-routing" "re-frame.routing"]

 ;; The greppable trailing token every thrown re-frame2 error carries.
 :message-token "[:rf.error/routing-artefact-missing]"

 :props {:to :fh.route/cart}}
